            "reverted_by": "Bhoimus",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#*Shaking can cause brain bleeding and even death.<ref>https://www.helpguide.org/family/parenting/when-your-baby-wont-stop-crying</ref>",
                    "#Learn the baby's cries. This will be hard at first, but a newborn is crying to communicate a need. As time goes on you will know the difference between each cry. Common reasons a newborn will cry include:<ref>https://www.helpguide.org/family/parenting/when-your-baby-wont-stop-crying</ref>[[Image:Handle a Newborn Baby Step 9 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Try the five S's. If you newborn is crying and you cannot figure out why, go through the five S's to comfort your baby. These activities mimic the womb environment and will help calm the baby.<ref>https://www.helpguide.org/family/parenting/when-your-baby-wont-stop-crying</ref>[[Image:Handle a Newborn Baby Step 10 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Recognize colic. If your baby cries for more than three hours a day for more than three days a week, the baby may have [[Soothe a Baby Who Has Colic|colic]]. All your attempts to soothe the baby will seem unsuccessful. Colic usually ends when the baby is around 12–14 weeks old. Colic usually stops on its own, but take your baby to the pediatrician if you are concerned.<ref>https://www.helpguide.org/family/parenting/when-your-baby-wont-stop-crying</ref>[[Image:Handle a Newborn Baby Step 12 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#*Shaking can cause brain bleeding and even death.<ref>http://www.helpguide.org/articles/secure-attachment/when-your-baby-wont-stop-crying.htm</ref>",
                    "#Learn the baby's cries. This will be hard at first, but a newborn is crying to communicate a need. As time goes on you will know the difference between each cry. Common reasons a newborn will cry include:<ref>http://www.helpguide.org/articles/secure-attachment/when-your-baby-wont-stop-crying.htm</ref>[[Image:Handle a Newborn Baby Step 9 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Try the five S's. If you newborn is crying and you cannot figure out why, go through the five S's to comfort your baby. These activities mimic the womb environment and will help calm the baby.<ref>http://www.helpguide.org/articles/secure-attachment/when-your-baby-wont-stop-crying.htm</ref>[[Image:Handle a Newborn Baby Step 10 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Recognize colic. If your baby cries for more than three hours a day for more than three days a week, the baby may have [[Soothe a Baby Who Has Colic|colic]]. All your attempts to soothe the baby will seem unsuccessful. Colic usually ends when the baby is around 12–14 weeks old. Colic usually stops on its own, but take your baby to the pediatrician if you are concerned.<ref>http://www.helpguide.org/articles/secure-attachment/when-your-baby-wont-stop-crying.htm</ref>[[Image:Handle a Newborn Baby Step 12 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
